A||N||14||FieroMaster88||How to find Modivation??||||5||
Z||000000||FieroMaster88||08-29-2001||04:59 PM||||Well...as everyone probably knows, I installed a V6 in my car.  It needs a lot of finishing up...like new wire loom, intake plenum and valve covers painted, just a lot of cleaning and such.  I feel like I am in the mood to work on it...so I go out to start and think "this sucks".  So I get nothing accomplished.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  What does everyone here do to get modivated?  I love my Fiero (and new V6) to death....just cant seem to get modivated.  I cant let my friends Civic EX's engine compartment look better than mine!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Here are a few pictures.  I will have more monday when i (hopefully) get more accomplished.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P8060001_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||5
Z||000001||OcalaFiero||08-29-2001||05:06 PM||||The motor looks great. That picture almost motivates me to pull out the Iron Duck from my '86 and drop in something a little bigger. Keep on keepin' on, it'll be worth it when you finish.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroMaster88||08-29-2001||05:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by OcalaFiero:<BR><B>The motor looks great. That picture almost motivates me to pull out the Iron Duck from my '86 and drop in something a little bigger. Keep on keepin' on, it'll be worth it when you finish.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah...engine conversons are fun.  I had a 2.5L with an automatic trans before.  Now I have a 2.8 from a 85 GT and a 5 speed isuzu.  Just dont try to install both in a week....it can be done, just is not much fun.<P><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||08-29-2001||05:27 PM||||Fieromaster... I can see why it takes time to find motivation- you're engine compartment looks pretty good to me!  My GT is my daily driver all summer, so when showtime comes around- there is some cleaning to do. But my engine isn't my highest priority- I don't even have a trunk carpet or gasket (thank God for the vinyl cargo cover).  Still mine turns out OK, but nothing eye catching- and the 3.1L looks totally stock anyways. I have to tell anyone that it's different at all.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/strut1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000004||skitime||08-29-2001||05:41 PM||||Last Christmas when I got my car it was pretty rough shape, I kept this picture if RossT's car on my desktop at home and work to remind me how good my car could look.  Thanks RossT  It also helps to find other Fiero enthusists that stop around to encourage you too. <P>The photo I used for wallpaper of RossT's car that I had on my computers for months. <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Red_GT_t-top_3-4_front.jpg">  <P>My car lately,<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7080038_3.jpg">  <P><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||1
